# Wallapop CDP workers

One Wallapop **account**, one `chrome.exe`, port **9222**, profile `ChromeCDP-Persistent`. Publish and sold are **separate windows** in that process (not a second port / second user-data-dir). Worker slots may run in parallel; the same slot is serial (queue).

Do **not** guess sold/unpublish selectors. Live DOM (2026-10-08, item seller): `walla-button[text="Marcar como vendido"]` in `[class*="ItemDetailSellerButtons"]`, then new tab `tsl-sold-modal` `#markAsSoldButton`, then `/app/catalog/sold` first `.CatalogItem__content--sold` href match. Never Destacar / Eliminar / Reservar / Cancelar.

## Workers (now)

1. **Monitor** — not built. Chrome stays up.
2. **Publish** — 9222 / `ChromeCDP-Persistent`. **Look at the SKU first** (title vs Tu Catálogo). Do not post a duplicate; Wallapop Follow-up may delete it after Yuhu. After Publicar: grab first `tsl-catalog-item` `/item/` href immediately (DOM under Yuhu), then dismiss «Ahora no, gracias». Close the publish window. Quit chrome.exe only if the sold slot is idle.
3. **Sold** (C8) — same Chrome, own window. Needs a saved public `/item/…` URL. Close item + modal tabs after the job. Quit chrome.exe only if the publish slot is idle.

Later: AI chat worker.

## After a job (chosen)

- **Publish / sold:** close that worker’s window/tabs. Do not `browser.close()` while the other slot is busy.
- **Monitor:** do not quit.
- **Login / logout / rehydrate:** exclusive; no worker slot starts until they finish.
